		"id": 1,
		"lang": "en",
		"title": "Building this site with Bun + React",
		"date": "2026-08-28",
		"tags": [
			"Bun",
			"React",
			"Tailwind"
		],
		"excerpt": "How I built this site with Bun, React 19, and shadcn/ui, including the MDX content pipeline.",
		"readingTime": 2,
		"html": "<h2 id=\"why-this-stack\"><a href=\"#why-this-stack\">Why This Stack</a></h2>\n<p>The bar for choosing tools is simple: <strong>the least moving parts, the fastest feedback</strong>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Bun</strong> acts as both runtime and bundler; one command to run, zero config.</li>\n<li><strong>React 19 + shadcn/ui</strong> keeps me from writing buttons and cards from scratch.</li>\n<li><strong>Tailwind CSS v4</strong> defines the theme with CSS variables; dark mode is almost free.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"the-content-pipeline\"><a href=\"#the-content-pipeline\">The Content Pipeline</a></h2>\n<p>The site is fully static (deployed to GitHub Pages), and every post is an <strong>MDX file</strong>:</p>\n<pre><code>src/content/&lt;category&gt;/&lt;slug&gt;.&lt;lang&gt;.mdx\n</code></pre>\n<p>The build script <code>scripts/build-content.ts</code> processes each post:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Parse frontmatter with <code>gray-matter</code> (title, date, tags, excerpt).</li>\n<li>Compile Markdown + JSX to React elements with <code>@mdx-js/mdx</code>&#x27;s <code>evaluateSync</code>.</li>\n<li>Render to a static HTML string with <code>react-dom/server</code>&#x27;s <code>renderToStaticMarkup</code>.</li>\n<li>Generate anchor ids with <code>rehype-slug</code> and collect headings into a TOC.</li>\n<li>Apply syntax highlighting with <code>rehype-highlight</code>.</li>\n<li>Write everything into <code>src/generated/content.ts</code> for the frontend to import.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"syntax-highlighting\"><a href=\"#syntax-highlighting\">Syntax Highlighting</a></h2>\n<pre><code class=\"hljs language-ts\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">function</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">computeReadingTime</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\"><span class=\"hljs-attr\">text</span>: <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">string</span></span>): <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">number</span> {\n  <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">const</span> words = text.<span class=\"hljs-title function_\">replace</span>(<span class=\"hljs-regexp\">/\\s+/g</span>, <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot; &quot;</span>).<span class=\"hljs-title function_\">trim</span>().<span class=\"hljs-title function_\">split</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot; &quot;</span>).<span class=\"hljs-property\">length</span>;\n  <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">Math</span>.<span class=\"hljs-title function_\">max</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>, <span class=\"hljs-title class_\">Math</span>.<span class=\"hljs-title function_\">round</span>(words / <span class=\"hljs-number\">200</span>));\n}\n</code></pre>\n<h2 id=\"gotchas-hit-along-the-way\"><a href=\"#gotchas-hit-along-the-way\">Gotchas Hit Along the Way</a></h2>\n<ul>\n<li><code>@types/gray-matter</code> does not exist on npm; gray-matter ships its own types.</li>\n<li>Running the shadcn CLI via <code>npx</code> crashes on a missing <code>@ts-morph/common</code>; using the local <code>bun x shadcn</code> works.</li>\n<li>The Tooltip component from shadcn requires a wrapping <code>TooltipProvider</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"summary\"><a href=\"#summary\">Summary</a></h2>\n<p>The payoff: <strong>content written in Markdown, UI drawn in React, single-pass build, fully static output.</strong></p>",
